In 1986, Donald McGillivray described two subspecies of G. baueri and the names are accepted by the Australian Plant Census:
 Grevillea baueri subsp. asperula McGill. is often an open plant with leaves {{cvt|5–10|mm}} wide, the upper surface rough with many granules, and has branched, down-curved flower groups;
 Grevillea baueri R.Br. subsp. baueri is often a compact plant with leaves {{cvt|3–7|mm}} wide, the upper surface mostly smooth, and has simple, erect flower groups.
